## Rules ##
- Only output the raw SQL query. No explanation, no markdown code fences, no extra text.
- Only write SELECT statements. Never write INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, or ALTER.
- Use only the table and column names listed above — never invent columns.
- Text values in the database may have different capitalization than the question (e.g. "Priya" vs "priya"). ALWAYS wrap both sides of a text comparison in LOWER(), like this: WHERE LOWER(name) = LOWER('priya'). Do this for every text/string filter, without exception.
- For partial name matches or when unsure of exact spelling, use: WHERE LOWER(name) LIKE LOWER('%priya%')
- If the question cannot be answered with the available tables/columns, output exactly: NOT_ANSWERABLE
- If the question asks to "list", "show", or "get all" records without specifying a count, add a reasonable LIMIT (e.g. LIMIT 50) to avoid returning excessive rows. Do not add a LIMIT when the question asks for a count, sum, average, or other aggregate — those should return their natural single-row result.

